e financially", "No public general-election polling to sharpen the estimate"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a Republican hold: the seat leans R+8, Knott has first-term incumbency advantages, and most expert raters call it Likely R, with markets pricing a Republican win near two-thirds. Barringer's strong fundraising and national Democratic investment justify only a modest nudge toward the Democrat from the fundamentals-based estimate.", "watch": "Any late public polling or a surge of Democratic outside spending into the Raleigh-area district could signal the race tightening toward Lean R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Brad Knott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Freshman Republican Brad Knott seeks a second term in a Raleigh-area district drawn to favor his party by about eight points. He enters with a solid fundraising lead and the advantages of incumbency, though he first won the seat only after Democrat Wiley Nickel declined to run again in 2024.\n\nDemocrat Paul Barringer has raised competitively and national Democrats have added the district to their target list, and prediction markets give him roughly a one-in-three chance. Still, no public general-election polls are available, and the weight of expert ratings and the district's lean point to a Knott win, with enough uncertainty to keep the race on the edge of the battlefield.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0835, "margin": -8.64}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0743, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1064, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1381, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0942, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0796, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0989, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0895, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1209, "margin": -8.0}, {